INT. VANTAGE LOGISTICS - CONFERENCE ROOM - DAY

A glass box with a long table and a screen. A "Q3 SYNERGY ROADMAP" slide glows. A bowl of unopened mints sits at the center.

GLORIA, 40s, regional director, taps a laser pointer on the screen. MURRAY, 50s, a senior manager, scribbles notes with a pen that has clearly run out of ink. Neither looks at the other.

GLORIA
We'll circle back.

MURRAY
We circled back last week.

GLORIA
We'll circle back again.

Murray presses harder on the pen. The pen refuses. He sets it down and eyes the mints.

The door opens. FITZGERALD, 20s, the new hire, in a suit too bright for the room, peeks in with a stack of binders. He has the face of someone who's been told "it's easy" many times.

FITZGERALD
Sorry. Is this the roadmap meeting?

MURRAY
It's the road. We're still waiting on the map.

FITZGERALD
Great! I brought binders.

Gloria and Murray exchange a look. Fitzgerald distributes the binders. He gives one to Murray, who weighs it as if it were a brick. He gives one to Gloria, who doesn't open it.

FITZGERALD (CONT'D)
So, where are we on the deliverables?

GLORIA
He asked about deliverables.

MURRAY
He asked about deliverables.

FITZGERALD
Is that bad?

Murray reaches for a mint. He unwraps it, slowly, popping it into his mouth. He chews. Gloria watches him. Fitzgerald watches both.

MURRAY
The deliverables, Fitzgerald, are the things we deliver.

FITZGERALD
And what do we deliver?

GLORIA
Meetings.

A long silence. Fitzgerald nods, writing it down.
